v10 — High-Assurance Audit + Medical-Oncology Project Discovery
Builds on the persisted v9 tables. Nothing in v8/v9 is overwritten.

This phase does NOT estimate comparative treatment effects. Outcome counts are used only for feasibility and power.

Date-shift framework (new REACH clarification)
All dates for a given patient are shifted by the SAME fixed duration, magnitude ≤ 6 months. Therefore within-patient intervals are exact and valid; absolute calendar dates are bounded: true_date ∈ [observed − 6mo, observed + 6mo].

Regulatory era is classified in three categories against each anchor date D: DEFINITELY_PRE_APPROVAL (observed < D−6mo), DATE_SHIFT_UNCERTAIN (within ±6mo of D), DEFINITELY_POST_APPROVAL (observed > D+6mo). Anchors: Atezo/Bev 1L 2020-05-29, STRIDE 2022-10-21, Nivo/Ipi 1L 2025-04-11.

Global safety rule
Every important derived result must pass CHECK A (computational invariant), CHECK B (independent source/algorithm reproduction) and CHECK C (manual clinical audit). Anything failing a check is labelled FAILED VALIDATION — DO NOT USE and excluded from project ranking.

